{"schemaVersion":1,"key":"intermediate/ui","track":"engineers","lang":"en","dir":"ltr","title":"Agentic UI","words":2882,"objectives":{"lang":"en","items":["Say what agentic UI is, and how it differs from a traditional UI and a chat box","Explain why an agent's run is streamed as events instead of returned at the end","Name the main kinds of event a run produces: lifecycle, text, reasoning, tool call, subagent, state","Explain the coupling problem that a shared event contract removes","Place AG-UI next to MCP and A2A in the agent protocol stack","Say what human in the loop is, and how an agentic UI pauses a run for a person's answer"]},"translatedObjectives":null,"prerequisites":[{"key":"intermediate/loop-engineering","number":14,"title":"Loop Engineering","drawn":true,"track":"engineers","lang":"en"}],"previous":{"key":"intermediate/loop-engineering","number":14,"title":"Loop Engineering","drawn":true,"track":"engineers","lang":"en"},"next":{"key":"intermediate/security","number":16,"title":"Security","drawn":true,"track":"engineers","lang":"en"},"toc":[{"id":"what-agentic-ui-is","text":"What Agentic UI is","depth":2},{"id":"why-stream-the-run","text":"Why Stream the Run","depth":2},{"id":"what-gets-streamed","text":"What Gets Streamed","depth":2},{"id":"every-agent-speaks-its-own-format","text":"Every Agent Speaks Its Own Format","depth":2},{"id":"ag-ui","text":"AG-UI","depth":2},{"id":"who-supports-it","text":"Who Supports It","depth":3},{"id":"the-agent-protocol-stack","text":"The Agent Protocol Stack","depth":2},{"id":"human-in-the-loop","text":"Human in the Loop","depth":2},{"id":"beyond-streaming","text":"Beyond Streaming","depth":2},{"id":"key-terms","text":"Key Terms","depth":2},{"id":"summary","text":"Summary","depth":2},{"id":"references","text":"References","depth":2},{"id":"-articles","text":"📄 Articles","depth":3},{"id":"️-tools","text":"🛠️ Tools","depth":3},{"id":"️-repositories","text":"🗃️ Repositories","depth":3},{"id":"-modules","text":"🧭 Modules","depth":3}],"body":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"intermediate/loop-engineering","track":"engineers","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Loop Engineering"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ended with agents that run for minutes, hours, and sometimes days. Someone still has to look at that work: see what the agent is doing, stop it when it goes wrong, and approve the steps that matter. This module is about the interface where that happens, and about the contract that carries an agent's work from the backend to the screen."}],"lead":true},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-agentic-ui-is","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"What Agentic UI is"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"CopilotKit's "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://www.copilotkit.ai/learning/what-is-agentic-ui"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"What Is Agentic UI?"}]},{"type":"text","text":" gives the definition that this module uses:"}]},{"type":"quote","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Agentic UI is user interface built for humans and AI agents to work in the same application."}]},{"type":"text","text":" It streams agent work as it happens, accepts human steering and approvals mid-run, renders agent-generated interface alongside developer-built components, and keeps application state synchronized between the user and the agent."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The difference from the interfaces you already know is who is doing the work."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"A traditional UI"}]},{"type":"text","text":" assumes a human who issues commands to software that behaves the same way every time. You press a button, and the same thing happens."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"A chat UI"}]},{"type":"text","text":" assumes one question and one answer. You type, you wait, and a reply appears."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"An agentic UI"}]},{"type":"text","text":" assumes an agent that is already running. The agent makes many decisions and calls many tools, and the human watches, directs, and corrects it while it works."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"This module covers the parts of that definition that every agentic UI is built on: "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"streaming the agent's work as it happens"}]},{"type":"text","text":", the protocol that standardises it, and "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"human in the loop"}]},{"type":"text","text":", the approvals. Steering a run while it works, shared state and interface that the agent generates itself belong to the Expert module, "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"expert/advanced-ui","track":"engineers","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Advanced Agentic UI"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-stream-the-run","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Why Stream the Run"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"An agent run takes time. A single answer from a model already arrives one token at a time, as "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"fundamentals/llms","track":"engineers","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"LLM Fundamentals"}]},{"type":"text","text":" showed. An agent adds more on top of that: it thinks, it calls a tool, it waits for the result, it calls another tool, and it may start subagents. The whole run can take a minute, or an hour."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"So there are two ways to build the screen."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Wait, then show everything."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The backend runs the whole agent loop. When the loop ends, it sends the final answer. The user looks at a spinner for the whole time, and has no idea whether the agent is working, stuck, or going in the wrong direction."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Stream the run."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The backend sends each piece of work to the front end as soon as it exists: a few words of the answer, the start of a tool call, the result of that call. The user sees the progress as it happens, the same way you watch a coding agent work in its terminal."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Agent products such as coding agents and chat assistants use the second way. The work is produced step by step anyway, so there is no reason to hide it until the end. Seeing the steps also lets the user catch a mistake early, while the run is still cheap to stop."}]},{"type":"image","number":"15.1","title":"A streaming agent interface","note":"The screen starts with an empty prompt. Once the agent starts, a checklist of its steps fills in, and each step is ticked off as the agent finishes it, so the user sees progress instead of a spinner.","src":"course-images/intermediate/streaming-ui.webp","alt":"A streaming agent interface","width":1280,"height":720},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-gets-streamed","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"What Gets Streamed"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The backend does not stream one long string. It streams "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"events"}]},{"type":"text","text":": small, typed messages, each of which says what just happened. For one turn of the weather agent from "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"fundamentals/tools","track":"engineers","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Tool Calling"}]},{"type":"text","text":", the stream looks like this:"}]},{"type":"diagram","number":"15.2","title":"What Gets Streamed","svg":{"light":"api/v1/diagrams/b4ecf6fa8a66eaad0a914f31e832dddb.svg","dark":"api/v1/diagrams/757f7515e944efe88a2cde26ddb8f841.svg"}},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The front end reads each event and updates the screen: it adds words to the message bubble as they arrive, shows a \"checking the weather\" card while the tool runs, and fills the card with the result."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The kinds of event are the same in almost every agent:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Lifecycle"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the run started, a step started or finished, the run finished, the run failed."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": a message started, a piece of its content arrived, the message ended."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Reasoning"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the model's thinking, streamed the same way as text."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Tool calls"}]},{"type":"text","text":": a call started, its arguments arrived piece by piece, the call ended, the result came back. This is the "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"fundamentals/tools","track":"engineers","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Tool Calling"}]},{"type":"text","text":" mechanism, made visible."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Subagents"}]},{"type":"text","text":": a subagent started or finished, so the screen can show the work it delegated."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"State"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the agent's current state, so the screen and the agent agree on what is true."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"every-agent-speaks-its-own-format","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Every Agent Speaks Its Own Format"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is the problem. The kinds of event are similar everywhere, but their exact shape is not. Each agent framework has its own event format."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"LangChain, for example, has its own "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langchain/event-streaming"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"event streaming"}]},{"type":"text","text":" API. Each model message comes with its text, its reasoning and its tool calls. The stream also reports the subagents, the state of the run and custom updates. Another framework uses different names, different fields, and a different order. (LangChain also speaks AG-UI, below, which shows how the industry solved exactly this problem.)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"That ties the front end to the backend. The front end has to understand the events of the one agent framework behind it. If the team later moves the backend to another framework, the front end has to be rewritten too, even though the screen is supposed to look exactly the same."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"In software engineering we always look for "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"decoupling"}]},{"type":"text","text":": two parts that can change separately because they agree on a contract. MCP did exactly this for tools, as "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"intermediate/coding-agents","track":"engineers","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Code Agents"}]},{"type":"text","text":" showed. You describe a tool once in a standard way, and any agent that speaks MCP can use it. The same idea, applied between the agent and the screen, is AG-UI."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"ag-ui","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"AG-UI"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"AG-UI"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is the "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Agent–User Interaction Protocol"}]},{"type":"text","text":". Its own "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://docs.ag-ui.com/introduction"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"overview"}]},{"type":"text","text":" calls it \"an open, lightweight, event-based protocol that standardizes how AI agents connect to user-facing applications\"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"It defines one shared set of events. A backend that emits AG-UI events and a front end that reads them can be built by different teams, with different tools, and still work together. So if you write the front end against AG-UI, you can replace the agent behind it at any time."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The events are grouped like the kinds above. Here are the main ones, as AG-UI names them in "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://docs.ag-ui.com/concepts/events"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"its event reference"}]},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"table","number":"15.1","title":"AG-UI","rowHeaders":false,"align":[null,null],"head":[{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Group"}]},{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Events"}]}],"rows":[[{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Lifecycle"}]},{"inlines":[{"type":"code","text":"RunStarted"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"code","text":"RunFinished"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"code","text":"RunError"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"code","text":"StepStarted"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"code","text":"StepFinished"}]}],[{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Text message"}]},{"inlines":[{"type":"code","text":"TextMessageStart"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"code","text":"TextMessageContent"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"code","text":"TextMessageEnd"}]}],[{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Reasoning"}]},{"inlines":[{"type":"code","text":"ReasoningStart"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"code","text":"ReasoningMessageContent"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"code","text":"ReasoningEnd"},{"type":"text","text":", and four more"}]}],[{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Tool call"}]},{"inlines":[{"type":"code","text":"ToolCallStart"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"code","text":"ToolCallArgs"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"code","text":"ToolCallEnd"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"code","text":"ToolCallResult"}]}],[{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Subagent"}]},{"inlines":[{"type":"code","text":"SubagentStarted"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"code","text":"SubagentFinished"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"code","text":"SubagentError"}]}],[{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"State"}]},{"inlines":[{"type":"code","text":"StateSnapshot"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"code","text":"StateDelta"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"code","text":"MessagesSnapshot"}]}],[{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Special"}]},{"inlines":[{"type":"code","text":"Raw"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"code","text":"Custom"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"On the wire, each name is written in capitals with underscores, so "},{"type":"code","text":"RunStarted"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent as "},{"type":"code","text":"RUN_STARTED"},{"type":"text","text":". The weather turn from above, as AG-UI events on the wire, one JSON object per event:"}]},{"type":"code","language":"json","lines":[[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"RUN_STARTED\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"threadId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"t1\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"runId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"r1\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"TEXT_MESSAGE_START\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"messageId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"m1\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"role\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"assistant\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"messageId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"m1\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"delta\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"Let me check the weather...\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"TEXT_MESSAGE_END\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"messageId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"m1\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"TOOL_CALL_START\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"toolCallId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"c1\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"toolCallName\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"get_weather\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"TOOL_CALL_ARGS\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"toolCallId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"c1\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"delta\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"{","role":"string"},{"text":"\\\"","role":"number"},{"text":"city","role":"string"},{"text":"\\\"","role":"number"},{"text":": ","role":"string"},{"text":"\\\"","role":"number"},{"text":"Istanbul","role":"string"},{"text":"\\\"","role":"number"},{"text":"}\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"TOOL_CALL_END\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"toolCallId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"c1\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"TOOL_CALL_RESULT\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"messageId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"m2\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"toolCallId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"c1\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"content\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"34°C\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"TEXT_MESSAGE_START\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"messageId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"m3\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"role\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"assistant\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"messageId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"m3\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"delta\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"It is 34°C in Istanbul.\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"TEXT_MESSAGE_END\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"messageId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"m3\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"RUN_FINISHED\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"threadId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"t1\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"runId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"r1\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Three things are worth noticing. First, the arguments of a tool call arrive as "},{"type":"code","text":"delta"},{"type":"text","text":" pieces, the same way the text does, so the screen can show a tool call while the model is still writing it. Second, every piece carries an id ("},{"type":"code","text":"messageId"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"code","text":"toolCallId"},{"type":"text","text":"), so the front end knows which message or which card to update. Third, nothing here belongs to one framework. Any backend can produce exactly these lines."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"AG-UI runs on the ordinary web. Its overview says it builds on HTTP and WebSockets. So the events reach the browser over a connection the front end already knows how to open."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"who-supports-it","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Who Supports It"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Because the contract is shared, many agent frameworks speak it. The overview lists, among others:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Partnerships"}]},{"type":"text","text":": LangChain and CrewAI."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"First-party integrations"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Microsoft Agent Framework, Google ADK, AWS Strands Agents, Mastra, Pydantic AI, Agno, LlamaIndex and AG2."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Community integrations"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the Claude Agent SDK and the OpenAI Agents SDK, among others."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"It also has client SDKs in many languages, from Kotlin and Go to Rust and .NET. The "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://www.copilotkit.ai/ag-ui"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"CopilotKit"}]},{"type":"text","text":" team develops the protocol together with partner frameworks, and builds its own front-end components on it. The source is on GitHub at "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://github.com/ag-ui-protocol/ag-ui"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"ag-ui-protocol/ag-ui"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-agent-protocol-stack","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The Agent Protocol Stack"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"AG-UI is one of three protocols, and each one covers a different side of the agent."}]},{"type":"image","number":"15.3","title":"The agent protocol stack: MCP, A2A and AG-UI","note":"The agent sits in the middle. MCP and A2A reach left, to its tools and to other agents. AG-UI reaches right, to the users in front of the screen.","src":"course-images/intermediate/ag-ui-mcp.webp","alt":"The agent protocol stack: MCP, A2A and AG-UI","width":1600,"height":923},{"type":"table","number":"15.2","title":"The Agent Protocol Stack","rowHeaders":true,"align":[null,null,null],"head":[{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Protocol"}]},{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Connects the agent to"}]},{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Comes from"}]}],"rows":[[{"inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"MCP"}]}]},{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"tools and data"}]},{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Anthropic"}]}],[{"inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"A2A"}]}]},{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"other agents"}]},{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Google"}]}],[{"inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"AG-UI"}]}]},{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"users, through the application"}]},{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"the CopilotKit team, with partner frameworks"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"They do not compete. A real product often uses all three: the agent calls tools over MCP, hands a part of the work to another agent over A2A, and streams everything it does to the user over AG-UI."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Do not confuse the three. Each connects a different side, and you have met the other two already: MCP in "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"intermediate/coding-agents","track":"engineers","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Code Agents"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and A2A in "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"fundamentals/multi-agent","track":"engineers","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Multi-Agent Systems"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"human-in-the-loop","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Human in the Loop"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Streaming lets a person watch an agent. "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Human in the loop"}]},{"type":"text","text":" lets the person decide."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"An agent that works alone will sometimes reach a step that matters, such as sending an email, changing a database or paying for something. With human in the loop, the agent stops at that step and waits. A person approves the step, changes it, or chooses between options. Then the agent continues from that answer. The agent still does the routine steps by itself, so the person only decides where a decision is needed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"This matters most for steps with real consequences. LangGraph's "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/interrupts"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Interrupts"}]},{"type":"text","text":" page gives API calls, database changes and financial transactions as examples of critical actions to pause before. A person who sees the step before it runs can reject it or fix it. A mistake caught early costs less. That is also why the screen shows the steps."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"An agentic UI does this in four steps. AG-UI calls the pause an "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"interrupt"}]},{"type":"text","text":", and its "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://docs.ag-ui.com/concepts/interrupts"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Interrupts"}]},{"type":"text","text":" page describes the steps:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The run stops."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The run ends with a "},{"type":"code","text":"RunFinished"},{"type":"text","text":" event, and the "},{"type":"code","text":"outcome"},{"type":"text","text":" of that event has the type "},{"type":"code","text":"interrupt"},{"type":"text","text":". It lists one or more interrupts. Each one has an "},{"type":"code","text":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" and a "},{"type":"code","text":"reason"},{"type":"text","text":", and usually a "},{"type":"code","text":"message"},{"type":"text","text":" written for the person."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The screen shows the pending step."}]},{"type":"text","text":" It draws the message, when there is one, and the controls for the answer: approve and reject buttons, or a list of choices."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The answer goes back."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The front end starts a new run on the same thread. This run carries a "},{"type":"code","text":"resume"},{"type":"text","text":" list with one entry for each interrupt. An entry has the "},{"type":"code","text":"interruptId"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"code","text":"status"},{"type":"text","text":" of "},{"type":"code","text":"resolved"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"code","text":"cancelled"},{"type":"text","text":", and the answer in a "},{"type":"code","text":"payload"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The run continues."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The agent reads the answer and goes on from there."}]}]}]},{"type":"image","number":"15.4","title":"An agent that stops for a person's answer","note":"The agent proposes a booking and stops. The time buttons appear while it waits, and the run continues from the click. In the second run, \"None of these work\" ends the booking.","src":"course-images/intermediate/human-in-the-loop.webp","alt":"An agent that stops for a person's answer","width":1200,"height":926},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"AG-UI also has a simpler way, which its "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://docs.ag-ui.com/concepts/tools"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Tools"}]},{"type":"text","text":" page describes. The agent calls a tool that the front end owns, for example "},{"type":"code","text":"confirmAction"},{"type":"text","text":". The front end shows a confirmation dialog, and the person's decision goes back to the agent as the result of that tool call."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Agent frameworks have the same mechanism inside the agent. In LangGraph, calling "},{"type":"code","text":"interrupt"},{"type":"text","text":" suspends the graph at that point. LangGraph saves the state of the graph with a checkpointer. Then the graph waits, with no time limit. Call it again with "},{"type":"code","text":"Command(resume=...)"},{"type":"text","text":" to continue. The value you pass in becomes the return value of the "},{"type":"code","text":"interrupt"},{"type":"text","text":" call."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"beyond-streaming","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Beyond Streaming"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Streaming and human in the loop are the base. The rest of the agentic UI definition builds on them, and the Expert module "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"expert/advanced-ui","track":"engineers","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Advanced Agentic UI"}]},{"type":"text","text":" will cover it:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Steering"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the user redirects a run while it is still working."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Shared state"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the screen and the agent read and write the same application state."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Generative UI"}]},{"type":"text","text":", and the specifications for it: A2UI, MCP Apps, OpenUI and json-render."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"key-terms","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Key Terms"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Agentic UI"}]},{"type":"text","text":": a user interface that humans and AI agents use together in the same application."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Streaming"}]},{"type":"text","text":": sending each piece of the agent's work to the screen as soon as it exists."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Event"}]},{"type":"text","text":": a small, typed message that says what happened in the run."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Tool call"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the agent's request to run a tool, with its start, arguments, end and result arriving as separate events."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Decoupling"}]},{"type":"text","text":": two parts that can change separately, because they agree on a contract."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"MCP"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the protocol from Anthropic that connects an agent to tools and data."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"AG-UI"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the Agent–User Interaction Protocol, one shared set of events that connects an agent to user-facing applications."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"A2A"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the protocol from Google that connects an agent to other agents."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Human in the loop"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the agent stops at a step that matters and waits for a person to approve, change or choose before it continues."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Interrupt"}]},{"type":"text","text":": in AG-UI, a pause listed in a run's "},{"type":"code","text":"interrupt"},{"type":"text","text":" outcome, which a person answers and the next run carries back in its "},{"type":"code","text":"resume"},{"type":"text","text":" list."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Shared state"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the screen and the agent read and write the same application state."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Generative UI"}]},{"type":"text","text":": an interface that the agent generates itself, shown next to components that a developer built."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"summary","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Summary"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Agentic UI is the interface where a human and a running agent work in the same application. Its base is streaming: the agent's work is produced step by step, so it is sent to the screen step by step, as typed events for the run's lifecycle, its text, its reasoning, its tool calls, its subagents and its state. Every framework has its own event format, and that ties the front end to one backend. AG-UI removes that tie with one open set of events, the same way MCP did for tools, and many agent frameworks support it. Next to MCP (tools) and A2A (other agents), it is the protocol for the third side of an agent: its users. The same protocol lets a run stop at a step that matters and wait for a person, which is human in the loop: the run ends with an interrupt, and the next run carries the person's answer."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Next: everything that made the agent harder to supervise also made it a more valuable target to attack. That is the subject of "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"intermediate/security","track":"engineers","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Security"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"references","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"References"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"-articles","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"📄 Articles"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://www.copilotkit.ai/learning/what-is-agentic-ui"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"What Is Agentic UI?"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the definition this module uses, and agentic UI against traditional and chat UI"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langchain/event-streaming"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Event streaming"}]},{"type":"text","text":": how LangChain streams the messages, tool calls, subagents and state of a run"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://docs.ag-ui.com/introduction"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"AG-UI Overview"}]},{"type":"text","text":": what the protocol is, the frameworks that support it, and where it sits next to MCP and A2A"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://docs.ag-ui.com/concepts/events"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Events"}]},{"type":"text","text":": every AG-UI event, with its fields"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://docs.ag-ui.com/concepts/interrupts"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Interrupts"}]},{"type":"text","text":": how AG-UI pauses a run for a person's answer and resumes it"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://docs.ag-ui.com/concepts/tools"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Tools"}]},{"type":"text","text":": how a tool that the front end owns can ask a person to confirm an action"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/interrupts"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Interrupts"}]},{"type":"text","text":": how LangGraph pauses a graph at a step, and resumes it with a value"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"️-tools","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"🛠️ Tools"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://www.copilotkit.ai/ag-ui"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"AG-UI Protocol"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the protocol from the side of the CopilotKit team that develops it"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://dojo.ag-ui.com/"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"CopilotKit Interactive Dojo"}]},{"type":"text","text":": live demos of chat, generative UI, human in the loop and shared state, to try in the browser"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"️-repositories","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"🗃️ Repositories"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://github.com/ag-ui-protocol/ag-ui"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"ag-ui-protocol/ag-ui"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the protocol, its SDKs and its integrations"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"-modules","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"🧭 Modules"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"expert/advanced-ui","track":"engineers","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Advanced Agentic UI"}]},{"type":"text","text":": steering a run, shared state, generative UI, and the specifications for it"}]}]}]}],"draft":null,"quiz":[{"question":"What does an agentic UI assume that a traditional UI does not?","options":["That the user types one question and then waits for one answer","That the software always behaves the same way after each click","That an agent is running, and the human watches and steers it","That the screen is drawn only after all of the work is finished"],"answer":2,"explain":"A traditional UI assumes a human giving commands to software that always behaves the same way. An agentic UI assumes a running agent that the human watches and steers."},{"question":"Why does an agentic UI stream the run instead of returning the final answer at the end?","options":["Each step shown lets the user see progress and catch mistakes","Streaming makes the model generate its whole answer a lot faster","A final answer at the end cannot carry the results of tool calls","A browser cannot receive one large response from the backend"],"answer":0,"explain":"An agent run can take minutes. Streaming each step avoids a blank wait and lets the user stop a run that is going wrong."},{"question":"What problem does AG-UI solve?","options":["It connects an agent to the tools and data it needs to do its work","It lets one agent hand a part of its work to another agent","It makes the model produce fewer tokens for the same answer","It gives all frameworks one shared set of events for the screen"],"answer":3,"explain":"Each framework streams its own event format, which ties the front end to it. AG-UI is one shared contract, so the agent behind the screen can change."},{"question":"In the agent protocol stack, which side of the agent does each protocol connect?","options":["MCP to users, A2A to tools, and AG-UI to other agents","MCP to tools, A2A to other agents, and AG-UI to users","MCP to other agents, A2A to users, and AG-UI to tools","All three of them connect the agent to its tools"],"answer":1,"explain":"MCP connects tools and data, A2A connects other agents, and AG-UI connects the users. A real product often uses all three."},{"question":"In AG-UI, how does a run stop when the agent needs a person's answer?","options":["It ends with a RunError event, and the person must start over","It keeps the run open and sends text events until the reply","It ends with a RunFinished event whose outcome is interrupt","It deletes the thread, and a new thread starts with the reply"],"answer":2,"explain":"The run ends with an interrupt outcome. The next run, on the same thread, carries the person's answer in its resume list."}]}